@titlepage
@title Esploro
@subtitle A file explorer in Emacs, for Lisp desktops
@end titlepage

@node Top
@top Esploro

Esploro (Esperanto for ``exploration'') is a file explorer.  Its window
is a frame of Emacs, built on dired, with what a file manager is
expected to have, for the mouse as much as the keys.  Its core, which
makes every change to files, is Common Lisp, and knows which window
has each file open.

Every change can be undone: copying, moving, pasting, renaming, a new
folder, the Trash and files dropped in are each checked whole before
anything happens, done in the background, and kept in a journal.

